        {
            "number": 4,
            "revision": "88f474db6aebde822c7b0d1d0e47be891e360cd1",
            "parents": [
                "a83bec20d5c3f96242f2b4b7ccca1761b0f62f5e"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/47/79447/4",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Rohit PAI ",
                "email": "rohitpai77@gmail.com",
                "username": "rohitpai"
            },
            "createdOn": 1743776840,
            "author": {
                "name": "Rohit PAI ",
                "email": "rohitpai77@gmail.com",
                "username": "rohitpai"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Myung Bae",
                        "email": "myungbae@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baemyung"
                    },
                    "message": "It looks like - `SubRequest` copies a portion of the origin Request, but not body (which seems good).\n- url\n- method\n\nHowever, I'm wondering how Oem route path can use the `body` if it is needed?  \nIt sounds like https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/77511 is passing only Oem portion to it.\n\nEven so, I'm not sure how much can be saved by copying only Oem portion vs the original Request body?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rohit PAI ",
                        "email": "rohitpai77@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rohitpai"
                    },
                    "message": "Original Request payload can be huge for request like firmware upgrade. OEM routes should not carry forward this payload. Making sub_request with only fields needed OEM can make sure any future addition to original http request will not create memory issue."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 10,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> I'm wondering how Oem route path can use the body if it is needed?\n\nBy definition it shouldn't.  A \"sub route\" is a piece of a json fragment.  It should never need the raw object (unless it's breaking a json abstraction, which we shouldn't support)."
                }
            ],
